{"book":"EST","chapter":10,"source":"hbo","verses":[1,2,3],"records":[{"id":"EST.10.1.s1","verses":[1],"source":"וַיָּשֶׂם֩ הַמֶּ֨לֶךְ אֲחַשְׁוֵר֧וֹשׁ׀מַ֛ס עַל־הָאָ֖רֶץ וְאִיֵּ֥י הַיָּֽם׃","gloss":"And laid the king Ahasuerus forced labor on the land and [the] coasts of the sea.","pieces":[[1,"King Ahasuerus imposed tribute on the mainland and on the coastlands of the sea.",null]],"L":{"1":"And King Ahasuerus laid a tribute on the land and the coastlands of the sea."},"R":{"1":"King Ahasuerus made the people of his whole empire, even those along the faraway coasts, pay him tribute."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o170100010051"],"choice":"tribute: forced labor or a tax owed to the king","alternatives":["forced labor"],"reason":"The word first meant a work gang or forced labor owed to a ruler (1 Kings 9:15, 21), and later a tribute or tax. Here it shows the king's power over all his lands, a fitting setting for Mordecai's greatness in the next verses.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o170100010071","o170100010072","o170100010082","o170100010091","o170100010092"],"choice":"the land and the coastlands of the sea: the whole empire, to its farthest shores","alternatives":[],"reason":"The coastlands are the shores and islands of the Mediterranean world, the far edge of the empire (Isaiah 11:11; 24:15). Together with the land the phrase means everywhere he ruled.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"text_variant","tokens":["o170100010041"],"choice":"Ahasuerus: the king's name as read aloud","alternatives":[],"reason":"Here the written Hebrew text has a shorter spelling of the king's name, and the text read aloud has the usual form, Ahasuerus. Both name the same king.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o170100010071","o170100010072","o170100010082"],"choice":"the people of his whole empire, even those along the faraway coasts","alternatives":[],"reason":"Readable explains the phrase as one picture of the whole empire (m2).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":"The greatness of Mordecai","status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"EST.10.2.s1","verses":[2],"source":"וְכָל־מַעֲשֵׂ֤ה תָקְפּוֹ֙ וּגְב֣וּרָת֔וֹ וּפָרָשַׁת֙ גְּדֻלַּ֣ת מָרְדֳּכַ֔י אֲשֶׁ֥ר גִּדְּל֖וֹ הַמֶּ֑לֶךְ הֲלוֹא־הֵ֣ם כְּתוּבִ֗ים עַל־סֵ֨פֶר֙ דִּבְרֵ֣י הַיָּמִ֔ים לְמַלְכֵ֖י מָדַ֥י וּפָרָֽס׃","gloss":"And all [the] deeds of his power and his might, and [the] exact account of [the] greatness of Mordecai to which made him great the king, [are] not they written on [the] book of [the] words of the days of the kings of Media and Persia?","pieces":[[2,"All his powerful and mighty deeds, and the full account of the high rank to which the king raised Mordecai, are written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Media and Persia.",null]],"L":{"2":"And all the deeds of his power and his might, and the full account of the greatness of Mordecai, to which the king raised him, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Media and Persia?"},"R":{"2":"Everything the king did with his power and might is written down in the history books of the kings of Media and Persia. Those books also tell the whole story of how the king made Mordecai a great man."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o170100020151","o170100020161","o170100020172","o170100020182","o170100020191","o170100020202"],"choice":"the book of the chronicles of the kings of Media and Persia","alternatives":[],"reason":"Literally \"the book of the words (or events) of the days\", the royal annals in which deeds were recorded, as Mordecai's warning about the plot was (2:23; 6:1). The wording is like the closing notes on the kings of Israel and Judah (1 Kings 14:19, 29).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o170100020111","o170100020112","o170100020121"],"choice":"are they not written: a question that means \"they are written\"","alternatives":[],"reason":"The question expects the answer yes. It points the reader to the official record, as the books of Kings do.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o170100020052"],"choice":"the full account: an exact statement","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word means an exact or detailed account; it is used in 4:7 of the exact sum of silver Haman promised.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["B","R"],"category":"word_order","tokens":["o170100020111","o170100020112","o170100020121"],"choice":"a statement instead of a question","alternatives":[],"reason":"The question expects the answer yes (m2); Balanced and Readable state it, which says the same in plain English. Literal keeps the question.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"EST.10.3.s1","verses":[3],"source":"כִּ֣י׀מָרְדֳּכַ֣י הַיְּהוּדִ֗י מִשְׁנֶה֙ לַמֶּ֣לֶךְ אֲחַשְׁוֵר֔וֹשׁ וְגָדוֹל֙ לַיְּהוּדִ֔ים וְרָצ֖וּי לְרֹ֣ב אֶחָ֑יו דֹּרֵ֥שׁ טוֹב֙ לְעַמּ֔וֹ וְדֹבֵ֥ר שָׁל֖וֹם לְכָל־זַרְעֽוֹ׃","gloss":"For Mordecai the Jew [was] second to the king Ahasuerus, and great to the Jews, and accepted by [the] multitude of his brothers, seeking good for his people and speaking peace to all his offspring.","pieces":[[3,"For Mordecai the Jew was second in rank to King Ahasuerus. He was great among the Jews and well liked by his many fellow Jews, because he worked for the good of his people and spoke up for the well-being of all their descendants.",null]],"L":{"3":"For Mordecai the Jew [was] second to King Ahasuerus, and great among the Jews, and pleasing to the multitude of {{gender:his kindred|his brothers}}, seeking good for his people and speaking peace to all his descendants."},"R":{"3":"Mordecai the Jew was second in power only to King Ahasuerus. He was an important man among the Jews, and his many fellow Jews thought highly of him. He worked for the good of his people and spoke up for the safety of all their families."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o170100030041","o170100030051","o170100030052"],"choice":"second to the king: the highest office under the king","alternatives":[],"reason":"Mordecai holds the place Haman had (3:1; 8:2), next to the king himself, like Joseph in Egypt (Genesis 41:40-43).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o170100030092","o170100030101","o170100030102","o170100030111","o170100030112"],"choice":"accepted by the multitude of his brothers: approved by most of his fellow Jews","alternatives":["accepted by most of his kinsfolk"],"reason":"The word means pleasing or well received. \"Brothers\" means his kinsfolk, the Jewish people, men and women alike. \"The multitude\" may mean the many, or most of them.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o170100030121","o170100030131","o170100030152","o170100030161","o170100030172","o170100030181","o170100030182"],"choice":"seeking good and speaking peace: working for the welfare of his people","alternatives":["his own descendants"],"reason":"To seek someone's good is to work for their welfare (Nehemiah 2:10; Ezra 9:12), and to speak peace is to speak for their well-being (Psalm 85:9; Zechariah 9:10). His offspring here most likely means his people and their descendants, not only his own family; the book had said Mordecai raised Esther but names no children of his own (2:7).","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["L"],"category":"setting_alternative","tokens":["o170100030111","o170100030112"],"choice":"his kindred / his brothers","alternatives":[],"reason":"\"Brothers\" here means fellow Jews of both sexes, so Literal uses the gender setting; Balanced and Readable say \"fellow Jews\".","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["B","R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o170100030121","o170100030181"],"choice":"because he worked for; all their descendants (B); all their families (R)","alternatives":[],"reason":"Balanced and Readable link his good name to his work for his people, which the Hebrew sets side by side, and read \"his offspring\" as the descendants of his people (m3).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"}],"words":{"1":[{"id":"o170100010011","text":"וַ","after":"","lemma":"וְ","morph":"C","gloss":"and","strong":"2050b","transliteration":"wa","lang":"H","parse":"Conjunction"},{"id":"o170100010012","text":"יָּשֶׂם֩","after":" ","lemma":"שׂים","morph":"Vqw3ms","gloss":"he.put","strong":"7760","transliteration":"yyāśem","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Qal · past narrative (wayyiqtol) · 3rd person masculine singular"},{"id":"o170100010021","text":"הַ","after":"","lemma":"הַ","morph":"Td","gloss":"the","strong":"1886a","transliteration":"ha","lang":"H","parse":"Particle · definite article"},{"id":"o170100010022","text":"מֶּ֨לֶךְ","after":" ","lemma":"מֶלֶךְ","morph":"Ncmsa","gloss":"king","strong":"4428","transliteration":"mmeleḵ","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine singular absolute"},{"id":"o170100010041","text":"אֲחַשְׁוֵר֧וֹשׁ","after":"׀","lemma":"אֲחַשְׁוֵרוֹשׁ","morph":"Np","gloss":"Ahasuerus","strong":"0325","transliteration":"**ʾăḥašwērôš","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · proper name"},{"id":"o170100010051","text":"מַ֛ס","after":" ","lemma":"מַס","morph":"Ncmsa","gloss":"a.tax","strong":"4522","transliteration":"mas","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine singular absolute"},{"id":"o170100010061","text":"עַל","after":"־","lemma":"עַל","